@startuml leader-mode-sequence
' Zangbundel - leader mode (kampvuurleider), complete sequence from app start to the end of a campfire.
' For assessment of design/guiDesign.md v0.8 (sections 4, 6.3, 8; decisions D-19..D-80)
' against design/ble-protocol.md v0.12 (protocol 1.0) and design/functional-requirements.md v0.10.
' Dutch UI terms in quotes. Decisions in brackets: D-nn = guiDesign, numbers = BLE sections, FR-* = FRD.
' Render (UTF-8 source, one run per format: PlantUML uses only the last -t flag):
'   java -DPLANTUML_LIMIT_SIZE=16384 -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tsvg leader-mode-sequence.puml
'   java -DPLANTUML_LIMIT_SIZE=16384 -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng leader-mode-sequence.puml

title Zangbundel – leader mode (kampvuurleider), from preparation to the end of the campfire\nguiDesign.md v0.8 · ble-protocol.md v0.12 · FRD v0.10

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI, Roboto, sans-serif"
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0B2545
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActorBorderColor #0B2545
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #0B2545
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #CFE6FF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #13315C
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #FF8A3D
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #FFF4EA
skinparam SequenceDividerBackgroundColor #13315C
skinparam SequenceDividerFontColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ArrowColor #13315C

actor "Leader\n(kampvuurleider)" as U
participant "Leader app\nscreens" as UI
participant "Leader app core\n(libraries, setlists,\ngathering engine)" as CORE
database "Phone storage\n(app-private)" as DB
participant "Library host (HTTPS)\nor a file" as HOST
participant "BLE: beacon,\ncarousel, GATT server" as BLE
participant "Singer apps" as S
participant "Assistent's app\n(a registered singer)" as A

== 1. App start ==
U -> UI : open the app
UI -> CORE : resume data present?
CORE -> DB : read persisted gathering (key, gid, name, tokens, seq)
alt crashed while leading, within the resume window (default 10 min)  [FR-GATH-13, 10.9]
  UI -> U : instead of the welcome screen: name, fingerprint, time since the crash,\n"Hervatten" / "Opnieuw beginnen"  [D-67]
  alt "Hervatten"
    CORE -> BLE : pre-start scan ignoring this gid; restart beacon, data sets, GATT server;\nseq + 1 so a burst follows  [10.1, 10.9]
    BLE --> S : beacon with the same gid → singers reconnect by themselves  [FR-GATH-10]
    UI -> U : the leader's page as it was  (continue at section 6)
  else "Opnieuw beginnen"
    CORE -> DB : delete resume data, keys and singer table  [FR-DATA-08]
    UI -> U : home screen
  end
else normal start
  CORE -> DB : resume data older than the window → delete  [FR-DATA-08]
  UI -> U : welcome screen: name + versionName, at most 1.5 s  [D-04, D-05]
  UI -> U : home screen: scanning; "Zelf een kampvuur starten",\nicon row: Bibliotheek · Setlists · Herinneringen · Instellingen · Over  [D-21, D-22]
end

== 2. Preparation: libraries (configuration screens, background image) ==
U -> UI : "Bibliotheek" → "Bibliotheek toevoegen"  [D-50]
alt online: URL of a repository, release index or .zbl archive
  UI -> CORE : add library (URL)
  CORE -> HOST : HTTPS: release index → newest .zbl  [song-format 12.6, 12.7]
  HOST --> CORE : archive bytes (checked against sha256 from the index)
else from a file (.zbl or zip from storage, share sheet, SD card)  [FR-LIB-16]
  U -> UI : pick the file
  UI -> CORE : add library (file)
end
CORE -> CORE : bound the input, read the manifest, verify every song hash,\nvalidate as section 11; library id clash → refuse (L006)  [song-format 12.7]
UI -> U : licence summary and full text  [FR-LIB-21]
U -> UI : accept
CORE -> DB : install atomically; record revision, version, source  [FR-LIB-15, FR-LIB-17]
CORE -> CORE : assign the next library colour (8 colour-blind-safe colours)  [D-51]
UI -> U : import report: imported · skipped (file, reason) · warnings  [FR-LIB-07]
opt later: "Bijwerken" / "Uit" / "Verwijderen" on a library row
  CORE -> HOST : fetch newer release (only on tap, or a Wi-Fi check that asks first)  [FR-LIB-12, FR-LIB-13]
  UI -> U : "wat is er veranderd": added, changed, removed  [FR-LIB-11]
end

== 3. Preparation: songbook ==
U -> UI : "Liedboek"
UI -> U : combined list of enabled libraries: colour square, title, language,\nusage "3× · laatst 12 okt"; library name added when a title occurs twice  [D-51, D-52]
U -> UI : search a word in the title (switch "ook in de tekst"), sort A–Z / Z–A /\nvaakst / laatst gezongen, chips library · language · tag · usage
UI -> U : filtered list; "Wis filters" visible while anything is filtered  [D-52]
U -> UI : tap a song
UI -> U : lyric view (day theme outside a gathering), song info available;\none button "Toevoegen aan 'Zomerkamp'"  [D-53, D-45]

== 4. Preparation: setlists ==
U -> UI : "Setlists"  [D-54]
alt new, rename, duplicate or delete (delete is confirmed)
  UI -> CORE : manage setlists
  CORE -> DB : store device-owned setlists  [FR-LEAD-02, FR-DATA-06]
else import a .zbs from a file or URL  [D-59]
  UI -> CORE : parse (song-format 13), resolve entries against installed libraries
  UI -> U : import report; unresolved entries kept as "niet gevonden" with the reason  [D-74]
else a setlist shipped with a library (read-only)
  U -> UI : "Dupliceren" → editable copy
end
U -> UI : open a setlist → "Liederen toevoegen"
UI -> U : songbook in editing mode: banner "Zomerkamp · 14 liederen",\na checkbox before every row (title, language, library colour and name)  [D-54]
U -> UI : tick / untick songs; drag to reorder, swipe to remove; "Klaar"
UI -> CORE : save
CORE -> DB : setlist stored
opt "Exporteren"
  CORE -> U : .zbs file through the share sheet (mail, messenger, files)  [D-59]
end

== 5. Starting the campfire ==
U -> UI : home screen → "Zelf een kampvuur starten"
UI -> U : gathering settings: neutral name proposed ("Kampvuur 20 okt"), join code or\nQR-only, setlist to start with  [D-25, FR-GATH-01, FR-GATH-05, FR-GATH-21]
opt battery saver on or battery below 30 %
  UI -> U : "Zet de batterijbespaarstand uit en gebruik een powerbank"  (starting still allowed)  [D-68]
end
opt the chosen setlist has unresolved entries
  UI -> U : "12 liederen, 2 worden overgeslagen" above "Starten"  [D-74]
end
U -> UI : "Starten"
UI -> CORE : start gathering
CORE -> BLE : listen ≥ 5 s for running gatherings (the home screen has been scanning already)  [D-23, FR-GATH-16]
alt a gathering is in range
  UI -> U : refuse: its name and "Meezingen" instead; no override  [FR-GATH-16]
else none
  CORE -> CORE : Ed25519 key pair, gid = SHA-256(pk)[0..5]; X25519 key ek;\nseq random, ts 0; copy the setlist into the gathering  [10.1, D-55]
  CORE -> DB : persist key, gid, name, code, seq, singer table (resume data)  [FR-GATH-13]
  CORE -> BLE : GATT server; beacon (connectable, high power); legacy data sets\nuntil refused (≤ 3); extended set if supported; carousel  [6, 7.1, 7.4]
  BLE --> S : beacon {gid, seq, flags, name} and carousel: state, info, setlist
  UI -> U : leader's page: leader bar "Kampvuur 20 okt · appel-vuur · 0 zangers · 0:00",\nsetlist block, every song below its separator, unresolved ones greyed with\nthe reason; buttons ▲ · ≡ · ▼ and the QR button; night theme  [D-55, D-56, D-57, D-61, D-74]
end

== 6. Singers join (leader side) ==
S -> BLE : connect; write Join (sealed to ek): sid, name, code, xk  [9.3]
BLE -> CORE : open, check code and capacity; store sid, xk; count
CORE --> S : Join response sealed to xk: result, token
CORE -> CORE : state: singers + 1, seq + 1, sign; burst  [9.4, 7.4]
UI -> U : leader bar "· 12 zangers"; live statistics: singers now, evening maximum  [D-61, D-62]
note over UI, S : The leader never sees a list of singers: only the count (D-73).\nDisplay names appear only on requests (D-63).

== 7. Showing the join QR code, at any time ==
U -> UI : QR button (above ▲ ≡ ▼)  [D-57]
UI -> U : QR code black on a white panel, brightness raised; name, fingerprint,\njoin code as text unless QR-only  [FR-GATH-19, FR-DIST-02]
U -> S : a singer scans it with the camera app → joins as in section 6\n(key pinned from the code, 6.5)
U -> UI : tap anywhere → page again, brightness restored
note over UI : The join code and QR-only are fixed for this gathering;\na change means ending and starting a new one (D-71).

== 8. Leading the songs ==
U -> UI : scroll; ▲ / ▼ move between separators on the leader's own page only  [D-57]
U -> UI : "Nu" on a song's separator bar  [D-56]
UI -> CORE : push song (lib, song, hash)
CORE -> CORE : song document (DEFLATE, framed); state: cur, title, seq + 1, ts ↑; sign  [9.5, 10.5]
CORE -> BLE : beacon seq within 100 ms; burst: state first, then 3 passes of the song  [6.4, 7.4]
BLE --> S : singers with the library use their own file; others collect the frames;\nmissing frames are repaired over GATT  [10.3, 10.4]
UI -> U : separator "wordt gezongen", previous "gezongen", setlist block updated;\nlive statistics: songs sung, duration of the previous song  [D-56, D-62]
alt "Nu" on a song further down
  CORE -> CORE : songs in between stay in the list, unmarked (skipped)  [FR-LEAD-03]
else "Nu" on the song being sung
  CORE -> BLE : re-push: seq + 1, 3 more passes; singers that have it do nothing  [FR-LEAD-06, 10.5]
else language button on the bar (only when another language variant exists)  [D-65]
  UI -> U : the bar shows the variant (e.g. "EN"); "Nu" then pushes the variant  [FR-LEAD-07]
else "Wis" (only on the song being sung)  [D-65]
  CORE -> CORE : state without cur, seq + 1, sign  [FR-LEAD-06]
  BLE --> S : header strip "gewist"; text stays on the singers' screens
end
note over U, S : The leader marks no line or verse: follow-the-leader follows song starts only (D-70).\nUnresolved setlist entries have no "Nu"; ▲ / ▼ step over them (D-74).

== 9. Changing the setlist during the campfire ==
U -> UI : ≡ button → sheet with tabs "Setlist" and "Liedboek"  [D-58]
alt tab "Setlist": reorder, remove
  UI -> CORE : update the gathering's setlist copy
else tab "Liedboek": a song → "Toevoegen" or "Nu zingen"
  UI -> CORE : add after the current song, or push at once (as section 8)
end
CORE -> CORE : setlist document changed, seq + 1, sign; burst  [9.5, 10.5]
BLE --> S : new setlist; singers still see only songs already pushed  [D-47]

== 10. Requests ==
S -> BLE : write Request 0007 (sealed): token, rid, song ref or free text ≤ 100  [9.6]
alt requests open
  BLE -> CORE : store as pending; group identical songs, count likes  [FR-LEAD-12, D-32]
  CORE -> CORE : rseq + 1, seq + 1, reqstat with the pending rid; sign; burst  [9.4, 9.5]
  UI -> U : badge on the leader bar: rows not yet handled  [D-61, D-63]
else "Geen verzoeken meer vanavond" is on  [FR-LEAD-13]
  CORE --> S : error 0x81 "requests are closed"; singers' request buttons disabled  [8.3]
end
U -> UI : drawer → "Verzoeken"
UI -> U : one row per song: title (free text in italics), library colour,\ncount "×4", time, requesters "Jip, Noor en 2 anderen"  [D-63, FR-LEAD-10]
alt ✓ "Accepteren"
  CORE -> CORE : append after the current song; status accepted with setlist position
else ▶ "Nu"
  CORE -> CORE : push at once (as section 8); status sung
else ✕ "Afwijzen"
  CORE -> CORE : status declined; row removed
end
CORE -> CORE : rseq + 1, seq + 1, reqstat; sign; burst  [9.6]
BLE --> S : every requester learns the outcome from reqstat, anonymously  [FR-REQ-05]
opt switch "Geen verzoeken meer vanavond"
  CORE -> CORE : beacon and state flag REQ_OPEN = 0; document 8 open = false  [6.1, 9.5]
end

== 11. An assistent (delegate) ==
U -> UI : drawer → "Assistent toevoegen"  [D-73]
CORE -> CORE : assistentcode: 4 random digits, valid 120 s, one at a time  [10.12]
UI -> U : the code, large
U -> A : reads the code to the helper standing next to the leader
A -> BLE : Control op 9 {token, cid, hc} sealed to ek  [9.8]
alt code correct
  BLE -> CORE : add the helper's sid to dlg; consume the code; seq + 1; sign; burst
  BLE --> A : state with own sid in dlg → tab "Leiden"; fetch document 8 (sealed)  [D-46]
  UI -> U : drawer "Assistenten": display name with "Intrekken"  [D-73, FR-LEAD-45]
else wrong, expired or locked (3 wrong tries)
  BLE --> A : 0x8E; the leader shows a new code if needed  [8.3]
end
opt the assistent acts (accept / decline / push a request, push or add a song)
  A -> BLE : Control op 1–8 (sealed)  [9.8]
  BLE -> CORE : apply as if on the leader's screen; seq + 1; sign; burst  [FR-LEAD-43]
  UI -> U : the leader's page and request list update as it happens  [FR-LEAD-45]
end
opt "Intrekken"
  U -> UI : revoke
  CORE -> CORE : remove sid from dlg; seq + 1; sign; burst  [10.12]
  BLE --> A : tab "Leiden" disappears; later Control writes → 0x89
end

== 12. The leader bar during the campfire ==
U -> UI : drag the handle on the leader bar, or tap it  [D-61]
UI -> U : drawer: time since start · songs sung · singers now (max) · link quality\n"goed / matig / zwak" · duration of the last song; rows Verzoeken · Assistenten ·\nDeelnamecode · Statistieken delen · Kampvuur beëindigen  [D-61, D-62]
loop while leading
  CORE -> BLE : every 30 s a 2 s scan for other gatherings  [10.1, FR-GATH-17]
  opt another gathering in range
    UI -> U : drawer row "Ander kampvuur in de buurt: '<name>'" (information only, no alert)  [D-68]
  end
  opt battery saver switched on, or the platform is about to stop the beacon  [FR-GATH-15]
    UI -> U : warning icon on the leader bar; nothing interrupts  [D-68]
  end
  opt statistics opt-in is on  [D-60]
    CORE -> DB : record: song identifiers, relative push time, duration, skipped;\nsinger counts; BLE repair and failure figures; versions (no names, no ids)
  end
end
U -> UI : swipe up, tap the lyrics, or "Nu" → drawer closes

== 13. Singers leave ==
alt a singer leaves on purpose
  S -> BLE : Control op 10 "leave" {token, cid} sealed  [9.8, 10.11]
  BLE -> CORE : remove sid (and from dlg); invalidate token; singers − 1; seq + 1; sign
else a singer walks away silently
  CORE -> CORE : no GATT activity for 10 min → removed from the count  [10.9]
end
UI -> U : leader bar count drops  [FR-GATH-12]

== 14. Ending the campfire ==
alt the closing bar at the end of the setlist  [D-69]
  U -> UI : "Afsluiten" on the bar "Einde van de setlist"
else earlier
  U -> UI : drawer → "Kampvuur beëindigen"
end
UI -> U : "Het kampvuur voor iedereen beëindigen?"  [FR-GATH-08]
U -> UI : "Ja"
CORE -> CORE : state status = 1, ENDED flag, seq + 1; sign  [10.10]
CORE -> BLE : beacon ENDED; burst of the final state; notify stay connections
BLE --> S : singers show "beëindigd", delete received songs, write their memory  [10.11, D-49]
UI -> U : summary screen: name, date, time sung, songs sung, maximum singers;\n"Terug naar start"  [D-69]
CORE -> DB : leader's gathering memory: name, date, participant count, titles sung;\ndiscard requests, the gathering's setlist copy, connection data  [FR-DATA-03, FR-DATA-06]
... 60 s: GATT writes refused with 0x88 ...
CORE -> BLE : stop beacon, data sets, extended set and GATT server  [10.10]
CORE -> DB : delete keys (pk, sk, ek), singer table, tokens, resume data  [FR-DATA-08]
opt statistics opt-in is on
  U -> UI : Instellingen → "Statistieken" → "Delen"  [D-60, D-62]
  UI -> U : JSON or CSV through the share sheet (mail, WhatsApp, Signal, files);\nthe app has no server and sends nothing itself
end
U -> UI : "Terug naar start" → home screen

note across
  Not in phase 1, by decision: no download instruction for singers (D-66, FR-LEAD-30 withdrawn), no singer list (D-73),
  no hand-over of the leader role, stop and restart instead (D-72), no change of the join code during a gathering (D-71),
  no line position for follow-the-leader (D-70).
end note
@enduml
